To calculate the Return on Investment (ROI) for Product A, we can use the formula: ~~	ext{ROI} = \left( rac{	ext{Sales Revenue} - 	ext{Marketing Expenses}}{	ext{Marketing Expenses}}ight) 	imes 100\%~~.
ewline 	ext{Given:}
ewline 	ext{Marketing Expenses for Product A} = \$2000
ewline 	ext{Sales Revenue for Product A} = \$12000
ewline 	ext{Now substituting the values:}
ewline 	ext{ROI} = \left( rac{12000 - 2000}{2000}ight) 	imes 100\% = \left( rac{10000}{2000}ight) 	imes 100\% = 500\%.
